==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|gawk|y}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡɔːki/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gawky.wav|a=Southern England}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɔːki|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[awkward|Awkward]], [[ungainly]]; lacking [[grace]] or [[dexterity]] in [[movement]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|title=Appalachian Children's Literature: An Annotated Bibliography|page=77|publisher=McFarland|isbn=9780786460199
|passage=The “'''gawky'''” illustrations look as though they may have been done by Belva Jean herself (Bulletin, Mar. 1989).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Ann H. Gabhart|title=An Appalachian Summer|publisher=Revell|isbn=9781493423095
|passage=The woman had barely come up to Seth&#39;s shoulder. Petite with curly blonde hair and a dimpled smile. Nothing at all like Francine with her plain brown hair and hazel eyes. Just looking at the woman&#39;s picture had made her feel tall and '''gawky'''.}}
# {{lb|en|Yorkshire|West Riding}} [[left-handed|Left-handed]].

